  "description": "A constant is reported only where deleting it, alone or with the others reported, leaves a program that builds and denotes the same value at every name it uses. A later constant of the block must then drop by exactly one, which holds for iota plus or minus untyped constants and for the plain name of such a constant, and must stay a valid constant of its type. A member whose deletion would move a later constant any other way, re-list it, push it below its type's least value, make an expression after it divide by zero or shift by a negative count, or break a repeated list of several names, is retained, and so is an unnamed first member whose list the next specification repeats. A member whose deletion moves no constant code names, or moves one only by one step under an alias, is reported, and so is a constant no enumerated type holds whose deletion moves no named constant.",
